Z||000000||Spektyr||08-16-2001||08:03 PM||||Well I finally magic combination of time, money and waiting for parts delivery and my Fiero's back on the road!<P>The poor thing has been sitting for about 2 and a half months waiting patiently for me to replace the blown waterpump, and stubbornly I insisted on switching to an underdrive pully at the same time (much easier to do both at the same time, btw).<P>Ogre's cave came in handy for refilling the coolant (even if I did leave the radiator cap off the front and tried filling from the back like a bonehead).<P>The 4speed V6 doesn't seem much if any stronger in 1st gear, but then it goes by so fast that there could be an improvement and I just couldn't notice it.  2nd gear is where I can really tell the difference.  Much smoother, confident acceleration and a gleeful tendency to squeal the tires.<P>Looks like the poor Lincoln is gonna be neglected for awhile...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||10
